WEBVTT

00:00.593 --> 00:09.450
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.593 --> 00:09.450
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.963 --> 00:18.535
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.963 --> 00:18.535
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.677 --> 00:37.252
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.677 --> 00:37.252
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.626 --> 00:46.812
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.626 --> 00:46.813
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.046 --> 00:56.179
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.046 --> 00:56.180
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.339 --> 01:05.446
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.339 --> 01:05.446
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.795 --> 01:14.843
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.802 --> 01:14.843
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.863 --> 01:22.838
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.863 --> 01:22.838
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.771 --> 01:30.691
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.610 --> 01:33.945
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.821 --> 01:36.003
Black Jack.

01:48.881 --> 01:52.092
Originally by Tezuka Osamu - The Sixth-Magnitude Star

01:48.881 --> 01:52.092
The Sixth-Magnitude Man

02:05.982 --> 02:07.107
It landed.

02:08.317 --> 02:10.444
Stay still, Pinoco-chan.

02:17.452 --> 02:18.994
Hey, now.

02:19.287 --> 02:20.996
Sorry.

02:22.790 --> 02:24.166
What's that?

02:24.375 --> 02:25.792
It's the festival vendor.

02:26.085 --> 02:27.461
Festival vendor?

02:33.176 --> 02:36.511
Sir, why are these pushcart shops here?

02:36.512 --> 02:38.180
We're getting ready for the fall festival.

02:38.264 --> 02:40.182
What kind of shops will there be?

02:41.059 --> 02:42.517
There will be lots.

02:42.935 --> 02:44.227
Takoyaki,

02:44.228 --> 02:45.062
cotton candy,

02:45.063 --> 02:45.729
candy apple,

02:45.730 --> 02:46.396
chocolate banana,

02:46.397 --> 02:47.314
yo-yo,

02:47.315 --> 02:48.675
and there will be fireworks too.

02:49.275 --> 02:50.525
Fireworks?!

02:50.735 --> 02:53.153
Ohmigewdness!

03:01.287 --> 03:02.746
Doc...

03:04.165 --> 03:05.457
I love you.

03:07.168 --> 03:08.168
Pinoco-chan!

03:08.169 --> 03:09.169
Stop!

03:09.379 --> 03:11.463
Wake up, Pinoco-chan!

03:12.173 --> 03:13.590
Doc!

03:13.674 --> 03:18.428
Sharaku and dragonfly and twirl and festival
vendors and there are so many!

03:15.836 --> 03:16.836
What's that?

03:18.429 --> 03:21.353
But takoyaki and candy apples look so good!

03:19.430 --> 03:21.353
Calm down and talk.

03:22.034 --> 03:25.811
A festival at the shrine and takoyaki and
cotton candy and chocolate banana,

03:25.812 --> 03:28.021
and goldfish scooping and there's toss the hoop too.

03:28.110 --> 03:30.107
Oh, there's a festival?
I definitely want to see the fireworks too.

03:32.235 --> 03:34.486
Let's go together, Doc.

03:34.487 --> 03:35.362
If I have time.

03:35.363 --> 03:36.827
Even if you are busy!

03:42.161 --> 03:44.496
The chairman at Mannaka Hospital passed away.

03:44.622 --> 03:45.956
Who's that?

03:45.957 --> 03:47.874
He was a major doctor at a major hospital.

03:48.084 --> 03:51.586
I was sent to Mannaka Hospital once,
but got kicked out quickly.

03:51.671 --> 03:52.963
Why?

03:53.715 --> 03:57.175
He only looked after the doctors he liked.

03:57.677 --> 04:01.680
It's none of my business, but that place
was full of those kind of doctors.

04:01.889 --> 04:05.559
Doc, would you listen to my wish?

04:06.269 --> 04:11.606
Buy it, buy it, buy it for me!

04:12.525 --> 04:16.737
We must elect a new chairman to fill
the sudden vacancy of the position.

04:18.281 --> 04:21.629
I suggest we elect someone from our current staff.

04:21.784 --> 04:23.785
No objections!

04:24.120 --> 04:28.790
There are many excellent doctors at this hospital.

04:28.791 --> 04:31.209
Yes, so let me nominate this man.

04:32.628 --> 04:35.589
This senior staff member has been
around for 20 years at this hospital,

04:35.673 --> 04:37.258
Dr. Tokugawa!

04:36.883 --> 04:37.966
Objection!

04:38.593 --> 04:41.636
If you go by seniority, we also have another
staff member with 20 years of experience,

04:41.721 --> 04:43.930
Dr. Shibata.

04:44.307 --> 04:50.062
But Dr. Tokugawa has fine respectability and personal
character, making him the perfect choice for chairman.

04:50.104 --> 04:57.000
But Dr. Shibata is very well-known from his
appearance on that TV health program.

04:53.926 --> 04:57.000
Signs: "Health Advice", "Dr. Shibata"

04:57.320 --> 05:02.032
But Dr. Tokugawa's Health Exercise books are best-sellers.

04:58.793 --> 05:00.173
Book: Dr. Tokugawa's
5 Minute Health Exercises

05:00.293 --> 05:02.092
Book: Dr. Tokugawa's
5 Minute Health Exercises 2

05:02.116 --> 05:04.910
Dr. Shibata is well-versed in accounting too!

05:04.911 --> 05:07.746
Dr. Tokugawa has political power too!

05:07.747 --> 05:10.040
Dr. Shibata does too!

05:12.859 --> 05:14.359
OK, how about this?

05:14.777 --> 05:18.071
Shall we have an election during the next staff meeting?

05:18.406 --> 05:19.364
Election?

05:21.159 --> 05:23.076
That may be a good idea.

05:23.870 --> 05:26.371
Yeah, that's it.

05:29.375 --> 05:33.962
I thought there was another doctor who
has worked here more than 20 years.

05:33.963 --> 05:35.422
Who was...

05:36.966 --> 05:39.009
Yeah, that's him.

05:39.260 --> 05:41.762
Oh yeah, there's Dr. Shiitake.

05:41.763 --> 05:43.430
I totally forgot.

05:43.431 --> 05:45.974
He always gets used like a doctor's assistant.

05:46.049 --> 05:47.829
Operation in progress

05:50.396 --> 05:53.398
Dr. Shiitake, please take care of the rest.

05:54.233 --> 05:55.108
Yes.

06:08.164 --> 06:12.584
Dr. Shiitake, my operation is next.

06:13.419 --> 06:15.253
Yes, I know.

06:20.885 --> 06:21.968
See you.

06:30.603 --> 06:31.603
Here!

06:31.050 --> 06:33.470
Sign: Koromo Kimono Obi

06:31.604 --> 06:33.522
Over here, Doc!

06:36.025 --> 06:37.192
Good!

06:37.610 --> 06:39.653
It hasn't been sold yet.

06:40.405 --> 06:42.779
I've got to have a yukata for the festival.

06:43.324 --> 06:45.325
This is what you want me to buy?

06:45.535 --> 06:46.702
Correct!

06:46.703 --> 06:49.541
Don't you think it will look good on my nice body?

06:49.831 --> 06:50.622
No.

06:55.712 --> 06:58.505
I want to have a nice body like those!

06:58.715 --> 07:02.950
Why don't you make that kind of wish
on a shooting star, not on me?

07:05.680 --> 07:07.222
Shooting star?

07:11.728 --> 07:12.602
Looks like an accident.

07:13.604 --> 07:15.097
People are trapped!

07:15.815 --> 07:17.232
They can't get out.

07:24.157 --> 07:25.198
You'll be fine.

07:25.199 --> 07:26.255
I'm a doctor.

07:27.118 --> 07:28.564
He looks conscious.

07:30.413 --> 07:31.621
Are you a doctor too?

07:32.206 --> 07:32.998
Yeah.

07:33.708 --> 07:35.042
Can you take care of him?

07:35.501 --> 07:38.003
I believe he only has broken his right tibia.

07:38.908 --> 07:40.802
Me?

07:41.132 --> 07:43.008
Is a broken bone outside of your specialty?

07:43.426 --> 07:44.217
No.

07:44.927 --> 07:47.095
Then would you?

07:48.598 --> 07:50.098
What a pain in the neck.

07:51.017 --> 07:52.225
My leg!

07:56.230 --> 07:57.606
What about him?

07:57.732 --> 07:59.798
His right arm is severely damaged.

08:01.819 --> 08:05.113
Either way, I can't move him until the crane arrives.

08:08.618 --> 08:09.701
Are they okay?!

08:10.828 --> 08:12.120
We are doctors.

08:13.998 --> 08:15.499
The pain must be severe.

08:16.000 --> 08:18.382
He may go into shock if we don't treat him.

08:18.836 --> 08:23.006
I'm sorry, but it will take a while longer
before the rescue team gets here.

08:23.299 --> 08:25.217
Then do you have some Xylocaine?

08:23.299 --> 08:25.194
Xylocaine is the brand name for Lidocaine, a local anaesthetic

08:25.218 --> 08:26.426
Yes!

08:27.720 --> 08:29.113
I'm done.

08:32.016 --> 08:33.934
Let's let the hospital take care of the rest.

08:34.102 --> 08:36.434
You're fast.

08:37.397 --> 08:38.814
Here's the Xylocaine...

08:40.525 --> 08:42.025
Turn your head to the left.

08:43.611 --> 08:45.696
You'll feel better soon.

08:50.910 --> 08:52.119
It's okay.

08:52.412 --> 08:54.621
This will make the pain go away.

08:55.331 --> 08:57.124
Let's wait for the rescue team now.

08:58.710 --> 08:59.937
The blood transfusion comes first.

09:00.128 --> 09:03.296
You will have to amputate his arm at the brachium.

09:08.803 --> 09:11.914
Doctor, can you stay a little longer?

09:13.099 --> 09:16.650
No, I'd better leave the rest to the hospital.

09:16.811 --> 09:19.021
I'm just a passer-by.

09:23.234 --> 09:24.882
He's gone.

09:25.111 --> 09:27.112
What are you going to do, Doc?

09:27.405 --> 09:28.107
Oh? Gone?

09:28.281 --> 09:29.323
Oh? Gone?

09:29.824 --> 09:32.159
Doc, where are you?

09:38.425 --> 09:39.333
Doctor!

09:42.128 --> 09:45.005
Excuse me, but which hospital do you work for?

09:45.715 --> 09:47.826
I work for Mannaka Hospital.

09:48.926 --> 09:53.513
Mannaka Hospital? Where you lost the chairman?

09:53.598 --> 09:54.471
Yes.

09:55.099 --> 09:57.856
So are you the new chairman?

09:58.227 --> 10:01.104
Oh, no, I'm just a regular doctor.

10:01.522 --> 10:02.808
Unbelievable.

10:03.900 --> 10:06.610
I watched you administer that shot to the brachial nerves,

10:11.032 --> 10:14.159
and you managed to finish in just three seconds.

10:15.119 --> 10:19.122
An ordinary doctor wouldn't be able to do it so speedily.

10:19.624 --> 10:20.946
Well, thank you.

10:21.209 --> 10:24.127
I have just done other people's
dirty work for years, that's all.

10:24.420 --> 10:25.504
No way!

10:26.130 --> 10:29.633
Why would a skilled man like you
be the one doing the dirty work?

10:30.134 --> 10:32.636
You should be in a much better position.

10:34.097 --> 10:36.807
Doctors are no good if they are overrun by greed.

10:38.226 --> 10:39.017
Excuse me.

10:45.108 --> 10:46.817
Doc!

10:48.611 --> 10:50.696
Don't leave me alone!

10:52.115 --> 10:53.323
Oh, sorry.

10:53.324 --> 10:54.374
The yukata, right?

10:54.534 --> 10:55.701
I'll buy you the one you like.

10:55.702 --> 10:56.618
Really?!

10:56.619 --> 10:58.203
Can I get geta sandals, too?

10:58.204 --> 10:59.204
Sure.

11:23.721 --> 11:24.413
May... Oh!

11:24.414 --> 11:27.833
I want to get taller, I want to get taller...

11:29.210 --> 11:32.004
Owie...

11:33.006 --> 11:34.423
Doc!

11:34.924 --> 11:37.217
Pinoco, what are you doing?

11:37.510 --> 11:42.598
You're the one who told me to wish upon a star.

11:42.724 --> 11:44.016
Oh, that?

11:44.309 --> 11:50.522
But the stars shoot too fast, so
I can't repeat my wish 3 times.

11:52.609 --> 11:55.169
Hey, what's that star called?

11:56.321 --> 11:57.613
That's Vega.

11:58.031 --> 11:59.823
What about that one?

12:00.116 --> 12:01.465
That's the Deneb of Cygnus.

12:01.826 --> 12:05.545
Then what about that little tiny one?

12:05.914 --> 12:06.735
I don't know.

12:09.834 --> 12:12.795
Nobody would notice if the small one went away.

12:13.713 --> 12:17.216
The darkest star that we can recognize with the
naked eye is called a sixth-magnitude star.

12:17.634 --> 12:20.138
A star that's 100 times brighter than
that is a first-magnitude star.

12:20.804 --> 12:22.647
A big star is first-magnitude.

12:23.932 --> 12:27.017
Sixth-magnitude stars are very faint, virtually invisible.

12:27.602 --> 12:32.104
But they look small only because they're very far away.

12:32.816 --> 12:34.107
Far away?

12:34.818 --> 12:38.028
The electric light is brighter when it's closer, right?

12:38.905 --> 12:45.407
Even though they're much brighter than first-magnitude
stars, only a fraction of light may actually reach the Earth.

12:46.538 --> 12:53.120
The much brighter star is labeled just
because it's further away from the Earth.

12:54.712 --> 12:56.630
That doctor earlier is like that too.

12:57.215 --> 12:59.508
A sixth-magnitude man?

12:59.717 --> 13:00.425
Yeah.

13:00.635 --> 13:02.256
He is skilled,

13:03.304 --> 13:06.808
but he won't get elected chairman of Mannaka Hospital.

13:07.308 --> 13:08.934
Why?

13:09.102 --> 13:12.104
Isn't medical skill enough?

13:12.605 --> 13:20.237
Fundraising and social skills shine
brighter in places like that.

13:21.739 --> 13:23.552
That's wrong.

13:24.117 --> 13:26.410
It won't do any good complaining to me.

13:27.120 --> 13:28.036
Stop it!

13:30.498 --> 13:33.015
Dr. Tokugawa! What's this money?

13:33.209 --> 13:36.672
You know that we're planning to
purchase a new test machine.

13:37.005 --> 13:38.338
These are the funds for that.

13:38.798 --> 13:43.510
So, you mean, this is the hospital's money?

13:44.512 --> 13:46.263
This is embezzlement.

13:46.639 --> 13:48.307
Don't kid me!

13:48.933 --> 13:53.562
A chairman should be able to adjust for this kind of money.

13:53.938 --> 13:56.523
I want all the votes from the internal
medicine department with this.

13:57.901 --> 14:00.235
I won't lose to Shibata!

14:00.236 --> 14:01.236
OK, then.

14:04.699 --> 14:08.118
So, this is the hospital's budget?

14:08.328 --> 14:13.540
Once I become chairman, we can
adjust the money log for this.

14:14.125 --> 14:18.003
With this, I can get 12 votes from the
surgical and urology department.

14:18.338 --> 14:19.932
OK, then.

14:19.339 --> 14:20.297
Did you call for me?

14:20.715 --> 14:22.424
Hurry! Hurry!

14:25.428 --> 14:28.305
Oh, Dr. Shiitake,

14:28.306 --> 14:32.226
I heard that you rescued a man from
the accident in town the other day.

14:32.227 --> 14:33.769
Are you trying to catch some votes?

14:34.229 --> 14:35.604
Catch votes?

14:35.939 --> 14:39.817
Are you trying to get some popularity
and become chairman?

14:40.401 --> 14:42.236
I have no such intentions.

14:42.612 --> 14:45.239
Then vote for me.

14:45.532 --> 14:48.408
I will choose of my own will.

14:48.409 --> 14:51.899
So, you're voting for Tokugawa?!

14:52.122 --> 14:53.831
I will be thinking until the day of the election.

14:54.332 --> 14:55.499
What?!

14:56.126 --> 14:58.919
Why do we care about Dr. Shiitake?

14:58.920 --> 15:02.214
Let's buy off some other more powerful doctors.

15:03.716 --> 15:05.717
Dr. Mohri, may I?

15:10.306 --> 15:13.600
Can I count on you at the election?

15:13.935 --> 15:16.562
Cast your vote for me.

15:17.730 --> 15:19.314
Vote for Tokugawa.

15:20.316 --> 15:22.526
Vote for Shibata.

15:23.820 --> 15:26.405
Don't worry and take it.

15:26.406 --> 15:28.407
But just vote for me.

15:35.331 --> 15:39.523
At Mannaka Hospital, there are many prominent
doctors involved in this bribery scandal,

15:39.711 --> 15:43.797
Doc, that hospital is on the news.

15:45.425 --> 15:46.425
Embezzlement?

15:46.486 --> 15:47.319
Yeah.

15:47.510 --> 15:51.973
They used the hospital's money
illegally to buy votes at the election.

15:52.223 --> 15:56.018
You get arrested for your bad acts!

15:56.019 --> 15:59.438
So, what about that sixth-magnitude doctor?

15:59.814 --> 16:01.315
Probably nothing happened.

16:01.816 --> 16:04.776
He's a dream-like doctor.

16:05.612 --> 16:06.904
Dream, huh?

16:07.405 --> 16:11.366
He must be shining much brighter in reality.

16:11.618 --> 16:14.036
Most of the doctors are being arrested.

16:14.037 --> 16:15.829
What are we supposed to do?

16:15.830 --> 16:18.373
And what are we supposed to do for
even the interim chair position?

16:19.000 --> 16:21.001
Um, what happened to Dr. Tokugawa?

16:21.211 --> 16:23.212
You're recovering well.

16:23.838 --> 16:26.632
But let's continue the use of antibiotics for a little longer.

16:27.008 --> 16:27.841
Yes.

16:28.009 --> 16:30.219
Um, what about Dr. Shibata?

16:30.720 --> 16:32.721
I will take out your drain tube today.

16:32.931 --> 16:33.722
Yes.

16:40.522 --> 16:42.898
Hurry, Doc!

16:46.611 --> 16:47.736
1 pack of takoyaki.

16:47.737 --> 16:48.821
2 packs!

16:48.822 --> 16:51.365
And put extra mayo too!

16:51.366 --> 16:51.931
Sure.

16:53.576 --> 16:55.160
You're such a pig!

16:55.870 --> 17:00.315
What? You're eating lots too.

17:01.084 --> 17:02.549
The fireworks are starting soon.

17:05.839 --> 17:07.589
Let's go grab a spot!

17:40.457 --> 17:43.208
Hey, Doc,

17:48.089 --> 17:49.423
What's going on?!

17:49.799 --> 17:52.009
The fireworks exploded on the ground!

18:02.395 --> 18:03.645
His body is covered with burns.

18:04.355 --> 18:06.273
He needs surgery immediately.

18:06.441 --> 18:09.151
Mannaka Hospital is the closest from here.

18:09.152 --> 18:10.110
That one?

18:12.155 --> 18:13.071
Dang it!

18:13.448 --> 18:16.450
Mannaka Hospital is running short on doctors right now.

18:16.743 --> 18:20.746
In that case, let's take him to the other
emergency center 30 minutes away.

18:21.039 --> 18:23.540
No, Mannaka Hospital will be fine.

18:24.542 --> 18:26.460
But the doctors there...

18:26.461 --> 18:27.294
They will be fine.

18:28.157 --> 18:29.922
If there aren't any, there's always me.

18:36.513 --> 18:39.348
Why did you bring him here now?

18:43.520 --> 18:44.978
His body is covered with burns.

18:45.146 --> 18:47.648
He's also in shock and has a broken
bone, but I've applied first aid.

18:47.857 --> 18:52.152
But most of our doctors have been arrested, and...

18:52.153 --> 18:54.285
Don't you have a veteran doctor?

18:54.864 --> 18:55.739
Do we?

18:55.740 --> 18:57.241
There's Dr. Maeda from ophthalmology.

18:57.242 --> 18:59.368
As if an ophthalmologist could handle a burn!

18:59.953 --> 19:02.453
Hey, could he be...

19:04.040 --> 19:07.459
Would you happen to be Dr. Black Jack?

19:08.717 --> 19:09.360
I am.

19:12.841 --> 19:15.759
We heard that you're a master surgeon.

19:16.052 --> 19:18.470
Would you handle this operation?

19:18.972 --> 19:20.764
I can accept it,

19:21.057 --> 19:22.808
but it will costs you 50,000,000.

19:22.976 --> 19:25.769
50,000,000?!

19:25.770 --> 19:28.272
It should be a cheap fee to
protect the glory of this hospital.

19:28.773 --> 19:30.445
So, what's your decision?

19:30.859 --> 19:33.652
Will you leave it at 50,000,000
and ask me to handle the surgery?

19:34.279 --> 19:38.949
Or will you take the patient to another hospital,
and lower your reputation.even more?

19:39.951 --> 19:41.076
What is the matter?

19:41.269 --> 19:42.744
Oh, Dr. Shiitake!

19:42.954 --> 19:45.456
Oh, he is a veteran surgeon too.

19:45.457 --> 19:47.708
But has he been the operating surgeon before?

19:48.042 --> 19:48.751
Probably not.

19:48.960 --> 19:50.870
Can we count on him?

19:51.129 --> 19:52.951
I'm very busy.

19:53.465 --> 19:54.711
Would you decide quickly?

19:54.841 --> 19:58.967
Pay 50,000,000, or have Dr. Shiitake do it?

20:06.519 --> 20:10.314
I have never been the head surgeon.

20:10.815 --> 20:13.484
He's gonna make excuses and turn it down.

20:13.485 --> 20:14.943
He's scared.

20:14.140 --> 20:15.277
I will do it.

20:16.779 --> 20:20.548
I will do it, as long as you all help me.

20:21.701 --> 20:24.077
Now, what's the situation for the blood transfusion?

20:24.078 --> 20:25.028
It's being prepared.

20:25.705 --> 20:28.874
Has the family of the patient been notified?

20:28.875 --> 20:30.268
Oh, I will check!

20:30.877 --> 20:32.669
Continue the blood supply.

20:32.879 --> 20:34.296
Get the tetanus toxoid.

20:34.798 --> 20:35.672
Are the tools ready?

20:35.673 --> 20:36.381
Yes, they are.

20:36.591 --> 20:37.674
Get the mesh ready.

20:37.675 --> 20:38.197
Yes.

20:40.595 --> 20:42.137
Doctor, the heart rate is...

20:42.597 --> 20:43.973
Increase blood-flow.

20:44.182 --> 20:45.682
Get norepinephrine.

20:45.683 --> 20:46.129
Yes.

20:46.476 --> 20:47.976
Hemostatic gauze.

20:47.977 --> 20:48.559
Yes.

20:51.397 --> 20:53.982
Doc, I'm tired.

20:58.112 --> 21:00.823
The people at the hospital must be
having an eye opening experience,

21:01.324 --> 21:03.710
about selecting their new chairman.

21:03.910 --> 21:07.913
But you became a villain in the process.

21:08.289 --> 21:09.942
You just don't get it.

21:13.628 --> 21:15.613
You're always like that.

21:15.797 --> 21:18.875
Always lonely, and always hated.

21:19.008 --> 21:19.917
Let's just go home.

21:20.218 --> 21:22.036
There's no place for me there.

21:22.512 --> 21:24.721
I must check the broken bone in his leg too.

21:25.223 --> 21:27.516
He said that he applied first aid.

21:28.693 --> 21:31.589
This is more than just first aid!

21:31.813 --> 21:33.320
The bone has already been re-set!

21:33.813 --> 21:35.131
That's him!

21:37.899 --> 21:40.988
A star's brightness isn't the same as it appears to be, right?

21:40.989 --> 21:42.197
That's right.

21:42.198 --> 21:48.506
See, Doc, that one over there,
shining all lonely - that's you.

21:48.705 --> 21:55.043
And the tiny one right next to it is me.

21:55.619 --> 21:57.530
Are you okay being a sixth-magnitude star?

21:57.714 --> 22:01.008
It looks small, but it really is big, right?

22:07.100 --> 22:19.055
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.100 --> 22:19.055
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.173 --> 22:24.172
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.173 --> 22:24.172
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.741 --> 22:31.210
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.741 --> 22:31.210
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.754 --> 22:37.212
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.754 --> 22:37.212
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.816 --> 22:40.301
being heated up by you,

22:37.816 --> 22:40.301
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.510 --> 22:48.287
so much that I change color

22:40.510 --> 22:48.287
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.372 --> 23:00.141
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.372 --> 23:00.141
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.349 --> 23:12.080
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.349 --> 23:12.080
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.320 --> 23:23.671
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.320 --> 23:23.671
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.857 --> 23:28.778
I couldn't be happier

23:23.857 --> 23:28.778
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:29.022 --> 23:34.155
How does it taste?

23:29.022 --> 23:34.155
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.652 --> 23:48.112
I hate my homeroom teacher, Mr. Muramasa.

23:48.792 --> 23:50.114
You escaped?

23:50.318 --> 23:51.281
Save me!

23:51.741 --> 23:53.158
Come on out, Sharaku!

23:53.952 --> 23:55.911
What happened at school?

23:56.454 --> 23:57.500
Nothing.

23:57.956 --> 23:58.497
Answer me!

24:04.546 --> 24:07.007
I will do it if you can pay.

24:07.632 --> 24:09.299
I won't do it if you can't.

24:10.656 --> 24:14.552
Next Karte - A Teacher and a Pupil

24:16.057 --> 24:17.850
Pinoco's Diary...

24:18.571 --> 24:21.197
Doctors are no good if they are overrun by greed.

24:22.597 --> 24:23.071
Excuse me.
